body:
Library agent-guide layout: the library layout ignores every top-level entry that is not part of the library structure (`library.yaml`, `slides/`, `sections/`, `themes/`, `media/`), including the author-guide pair — `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` (the library/template-author full guide, library-agent-guide) and `AGENTS.md` (its reference pointer, agent-guide-reference). A library root may hold `AGENTS_KALIDE.md` and `AGENTS.md` alongside `library.yaml`, `slides/`, `sections/`, `themes/` and `media/`; they stay inert — never parsed as YAML/template, validated, rendered, listed or served — and are not template assets. The loader validates only the library structure (templates-dir-layout), so the guide pair and any other unrelated top-level entry (a `.git/` directory, a README, a notes file) load cleanly with no special case. The rule is specific to the library (templates) root; the deck root has no top-level-entry rule and its `AGENTS_KALIDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` are unaffected.

AC:
- `kalide init-library ../lib` writes `../lib/AGENTS_KALIDE.md` and `../lib/AGENTS.md` and `../lib` still loads cleanly (templates-dir-validation);
- a library root holding an unrelated top-level entry (e.g. `.git/`, `README.md`, `notes.txt`) still loads cleanly and that entry is ignored;
- `../lib/AGENTS_KALIDE.md` and `../lib/AGENTS.md` are inert to load/validate/render/serve/list (the guide files are not template assets).
